{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Deborah, Rebekah's nurse, died.</b> This verse is inserted between כי שם נגלו אליו האלהים and וירא אלהים אל יעקב עוד, and this supports the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory concerning the verse ותמת דבורה מינקת רבקה — that it alludes to the death of Rebekah; therefore he called the name of the place אלון בכות. And thus the Ramban of blessed memory wrote: it is not fitting to weep so much over an old nurse that one would name the place after her; rather, Jacob mourned and wept for his mother, whose love had sent him there, and she did not merit to see him on his return — and behold, Deborah was with Jacob. And on account of this allusion HaShem, blessed be He, revealed Himself to him to comfort him; and so they said of blessed memory: 'ויברך אותו — He blessed him with the blessing of mourners.' And so they expounded the verse (Genesis 25:11): ויהי אחרי מות אברהם ויברך אלהים את יצחק בנו. And what strengthens this is what is said shortly after: ויבא יעקב אל יצחק אביו ממרא קרית הארבע — and had Rebekah his mother been alive, it should have said, 'and Jacob came to Isaac his father and to his mother,' since she was the one who sent him there and Isaac commanded him thus at her advice; but because she died ingloriously, Scripture concealed her death." "<b>And thus</b> they said in the Midrash: You find that when Rebekah died, they said, 'Who will go out for her?' Abraham had died, Isaac sat in the house and his eyes were dim, Jacob had gone to Paddan-aram — who will go out for her? Esav the wicked — and they would say a beraita, 'they bedeck a despised one,' for then they would mock her. What did they do? They took her bier out at night. R. Yosi ben Chanina said: because they took her bier out at night, the Scriptures did not publicize her death except indirectly. This is what is written: ויקרא שמו אלון בכות — 'two weepings': one over her death and one because she died ingloriously."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:50.034314176Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}